{"id":"arimathea","name":"Arimathea","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:arimathea"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Arimathea","text":"A “city of the Jews” (Luke 23:51), the birth-place of Joseph in whose sepulchre our Lord was laid (Matt. 27:57, 60; John 19:38). It is probably the same place as Ramathaim in Ephraim, and the birth-place of Samuel (1 Sam. 1:1, 19). Others identify it with Ramleh in Dan, or Rama (q.v.) in Benjamin (Matt. 2:18)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G707","lemma":"Ἀριμαθαία","xlit":"Arimathaía","gloss":"Arimathæa , a place in Palestine","kjv":"Arimathæa","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"G2501","lemma":"Ἰωσήφ","xlit":"Iōsḗph","gloss":"Joseph, the name of seven Israelites","kjv":"Joseph","count":3,"share":0.75},{"strong":"G4327","lemma":"προσδέχομαι","xlit":"prosdéchomai","gloss":"to admit endurance)","kjv":"accept, allow, look  for, take","count":2,"share":0.5},{"strong":"G4091","lemma":"Πιλᾶτος","xlit":"Pilâtos","gloss":"close-pressed","kjv":"Pilate","count":2,"share":0.5},{"strong":"G4983","lemma":"σῶμα","xlit":"sōma","gloss":"the body , used in a very wide application, literally or","kjv":"bodily, body, slave","count":2,"share":0.5},{"strong":"G932","lemma":"βασιλεία","xlit":"basileía","gloss":"royalty","kjv":"kingdom, + reign","count":2,"share":0.5}],"verses":["Matt.27.57","Mark.15.43","Luke.23.51","John.19.38"],"related":[{"id":"pilate-pontius","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.094,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"}],"works":[]}
